+/*
+ * Open Citadel patch: a phonemizer is never disposed.
+ *
+ * Disposing one frees its neural G2P model (an ExecuTorch Module), and on some
+ * Android phones `Module::~Module` segfaults right there and takes the app
+ * with it (Play Console: PhonemizerHostObject dispose -> ~NeuralPhonemizer ->
+ * ~Module). So each phonemizer is made once per config and runtime, shared by
+ * every Kokoro pipeline built over that config, and kept referenced for the
+ * life of the process: a dropped reference would run the same destructor when
+ * the garbage collector frees the host object. A pipeline's own `dispose`
+ * still frees its two models and its tensors, which is where the memory is.
+ *
